, you know the feeling: code appears in minutes, but verification, integrat=
ion, and accountability for what the machine wrote eat up the rest of the d=
ay. <mark class=3D"zu zv af">In teams with high AI adoption, pull request r=
eview time grew by nearly 91% =E2=80=94 that=E2=80=99s Faros AI data from o=
ver 10,000 developers and 1,255 teams.</mark></p><p id=3D"564a" class=3D"pw=
-post-body-paragraph ox oy jl oz b ke pa pb pc kh pd pe pf fn pg ph pi fq p=
j pk pl ft pm pn po pp ha cv" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">Picture the sa=
me developer, two days of work. In 2019: eight hours in the editor, debuggi=
ng line by line, miles of boilerplate. Today: an hour writing a specificati=
on, three agent instances running in the background, the rest of the day re=
ading and accepting what they generated. <strong class=3D"oz jm">This isn=
=E2=80=99t less work =E2=80=94 it=E2=80=99s different work.</strong> And in=
 the next ten minutes, you=E2=80=99ll see exactly how it=E2=80=99s changing=
, which skills now decide careers, which don=E2=80=99t =E2=80=94 and how to=
 prepare yourself and your team.</p><h2 id=3D"d3a3" class=3D"pq pr jl z ps =
